[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Modules","page":"API","text":"Order = [:module]","title":"Modules"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Types-and-constants","page":"API","text":"Order = [:type, :constant]","title":"Types and constants"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Functions-and-macros","page":"API","text":"Order = [:macro, :function]","title":"Functions and macros"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Documentation","page":"API","text":"","title":"Documentation"},{"category":"module","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.LegendMachineLearning","page":"API","text":"LegendMachineLearning\n\nMachine learning algorithms for the LEGEND experiment.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.LegendMachineLearning"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.AbstractFeatureExtractor","page":"API","text":"abstract type AbstractFeatureExtractor\n\nMaps an array of waveforms to a feature matrix with one row per waveform. Subtypes implement features(fe, wvfs).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.AbstractFeatureExtractor"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.ClusterResult","page":"API","text":"ClusterResult\n\nAffinity-propagation result on a WaveformSample: assignment[i] is the cluster index of sample row i, exemplars[k] is the sample row of the exemplar of cluster k.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.ClusterResult"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.HaarFeatures","page":"API","text":"HaarFeatures(; n_samples=256, normalize=true, bl_window=0.0u\"µs\"..25.0u\"µs\")\n\nFeature extractor: baseline subtraction (mean over bl_window), repeated pairwise Haar averaging down to n_samples samples, and, if normalize, division of each waveform by the larger absolute value of its extrema. The number of Haar passes is derived from the input length, so one extractor handles presummed and full-resolution waveforms of the same detector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.HaarFeatures"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.LegendMLModel","page":"API","text":"LegendMLModel\n\nA fitted MLJ machine together with the feature extractor it was trained on, the label-to-category table, and provenance metadata. Calling the model on waveforms returns integer labels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.LegendMLModel"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.WaveformSample","page":"API","text":"WaveformSample\n\nWaveforms selected for training together with everything needed to trace each one back to its raw event. stratum names the selection rule each row was drawn by. All vectors share the same axes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.WaveformSample"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.MODEL_FORMAT_VERSION","page":"API","text":"Layout version of the JLD2 model file; loading a different version is an error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.MODEL_FORMAT_VERSION"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.UNLABELED","page":"API","text":"Label value of an exemplar that has not been assigned a category yet.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.UNLABELED"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning._detector_sample-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.LegendData, AbstractVector{LegendDataManagement.FileKey}, Any, Integer, NamedTuple, Symbol, Any}","page":"API","text":"_detector_sample(data, filekeys, row, n_det, strata, waveform_column, rng)\n    -> (; sample, stats, n_scan, n_matched)\n\nn_det rows for the detector of row, drawn in two passes. The scalar scan of filekeys gives the candidate rows; rows flagged by an aux trigger named in strata.exclude leave the pool, and add_pool_columns places the rest within it. scan_rows picks strata.n_scan pool rows, triggered ones first; their waveforms are read back from each file by timestamp and summarized by waveform_stats. From these scan rows select_indices draws n_det by strata.rules, and the sample takes the waveforms already read.\n\nstats holds, for the sample rows, the rule inputs the sample does not carry: the saturation counts, the pool columns and the waveform statistics. n_scan is the number of scan rows and n_matched the number of them each rule selects.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning._detector_sample"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning._grid_rows-Tuple{AbstractMatrix}","page":"API","text":"YAML/PropDict cannot serialize a Matrix; the scan grid goes in as one vector per row.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning._grid_rows"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.add_pool_columns-Tuple{Any}","page":"API","text":"add_pool_columns(pool) -> TypedTables.Table\n\npool (a table with filekey, baseline and daqenergy columns) with two columns that place each row within the pool:\n\nbaseline_dev: |baseline - m| in units of the median of these absolute deviations over the pool, where m is the median baseline of the pool rows of the same filekey. The FPGA baseline drifts from file to file, so each row is compared with its own file. When more than half the pool sits exactly on its file median the unit is zero, and the column holds NaN and Inf.\ndaqenergy_rank: empirical quantile of daqenergy among the pool rows with daqenergy > 0, in (0, 1]; 0 for the other rows.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.add_pool_columns"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.build_sample-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.LegendData, LegendDataManagement.FileKey, PropDicts.PropDict}","page":"API","text":"build_sample(data, filekey, config; rng, chinfo, filekeys) -> (; sample, stats, n_scan, n_matched)\n\nSample for the period and category of filekey: config.n_max waveforms split equally over config.detectors, each drawn by _detector_sample from the raw files filekeys and read from config.waveform_column. A detector whose pool falls short of its share of config.n_max contributes all of it and @warns about the shortfall instead of silently returning fewer rows than the caller might expect.\n\nconfig.strata holds the selection parameters:\n\naux_triggers maps flag names to the detector ids of the aux trigger channels, ts_window is the coincidence window in µs by which their triggers are matched to the detector's events (125 when absent), and exclude lists the flags whose events stay out of the pool;\nn_scan is the number of pool rows per detector whose waveforms are read and summarized, rows with daqenergy > 0 first (see scan_rows; 200 000 when absent, at least the per-detector share of n_max);\nbl_window and tail_window ([start, stop] in µs, required) are the windows of waveform_stats;\nrules is a list of {name, select, fraction} with select a LEGEND Julia expression over the columns of the scan table (see rule_predicate), and uniform the expression of the rows the remainder is drawn from (\"daqenergy > 0\" when absent). See select_indices.\n\nThe scan table has the columns of scan_candidates and add_pool_columns and those of waveform_stats.\n\nReturns the sample, the rule inputs of its rows (stats, one row per sample row), and per detector the number of scan rows (n_scan) and the number of them each rule selects (n_matched), both as PropDicts keyed by detector.\n\nfilekeys defaults to the raw files of every analysis run of the period, so rows may come from any run of it; filekey itself only names the period and the category. chinfo supplies the detector, channel and det_type columns used to look up each entry of config.detectors; it defaults to the full channel map of filekey. Pass any other table with those three columns to run without a channel map, e.g. a hand-built TypedTables.Table against raw files that predate or lack channel-map coverage.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.build_sample"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.class_fractions-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}, Dict{Int64, Symbol}}","page":"API","text":"class_fractions(labels, categories) -> Dict{Int,Float64}\n\nFraction of each configured category among labels; categories that do not occur get 0. Throws on labels outside the table or an empty labels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.class_fractions"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.class_weights-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}}","page":"API","text":"class_weights(y) -> Dict{Int,Float64}\n\nInverse-frequency class weights, normalized so their mean is 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.class_weights"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.cluster_result-Tuple{PropDicts.PropDict, AbstractVector{<:Integer}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}","page":"API","text":"cluster_result(props::PropDict, assignment, exemplars) -> ClusterResult\n\nInverse of cluster_result_to_props combined with the arrays from read_sample.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.cluster_result"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.cluster_result_to_props-Tuple{ClusterResult}","page":"API","text":"cluster_result_to_props(c::ClusterResult) -> PropDict\n\nHyperparameters, converged and iterations as a parameter-database entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.cluster_result_to_props"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.features-Tuple{HaarFeatures, AbstractVector{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform}}","page":"API","text":"features(fe::HaarFeatures, wvfs::AbstractVector{<:RDWaveform}) -> Matrix{Float32}\n\nFeature matrix of size (length(wvfs), fe.n_samples).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.features"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.features_config-Tuple{PropDicts.PropDict}","page":"API","text":"features_config(config::PropDict) -> HaarFeatures\n\nFeature extractor from config.features (n_samples, normalize, bl_window = [start, stop] in µs).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.features_config"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.file_sha256-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API","text":"SHA-256 of the file at path, as a lowercase hex string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.file_sha256"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.fit_affinity_propagation-Tuple{AbstractMatrix}","page":"API","text":"fit_affinity_propagation(X; damp, preference, preference_quantile=NaN, maxiter=1000, tol=1e-6, metric=Cityblock(), S=nothing) -> ClusterResult\n\nFit affinity propagation on the rows of X at a single (damp, preference) grid point. Cluster k is the cluster containing exemplar exemplars[k]. S, when given, is the shared similarity matrix from scan_affinity_propagation, reused instead of recomputed; its diagonal is overwritten with preference on every call.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.fit_affinity_propagation"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.flag_coincident-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"API","text":"flag_coincident(ts, aux_ts, window) -> Vector{Bool}\n\nTrue at each entry of ts that lies within window of some entry of aux_ts. aux_ts must be sorted, ts need not be.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.flag_coincident"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.haar_passes-Tuple{HaarFeatures, Integer}","page":"API","text":"haar_passes(fe::HaarFeatures, n_input::Integer) -> Int\n\nNumber of pairwise Haar averaging passes that bring n_input samples down to fe.n_samples. Each pass halves the length, rounding up, so an odd length such as 781 reaches 196 in two passes. Throws when no number of passes reaches fe.n_samples exactly.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.haar_passes"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.load_model-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API","text":"load_model(path; expected_sha256=nothing) -> LegendMLModel\n\nRead a model written by save_model. When expected_sha256 is given the file digest must match it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.load_model"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.load_qc_model-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.LegendData, LegendDataManagement.FileKey}","page":"API","text":"load_qc_model(data, filekey) -> LegendMLModel or missing\n\nModel valid for filekey. missing when no rpars.ml validity entry covers it. Errors when the resolved entry has no training_filekey (it was not written by the QC training step), was trained in another period, or the model file digest does not match the entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.load_qc_model"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.model_pars_entry-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.FileKey, AbstractString, NamedTuple, LegendMLModel}","page":"API","text":"model_pars_entry(training_fk, sha256, train_report, model) -> PropDict\n\nEntry written to rpars.ml by the training step. It names the training filekey (from which the model path follows), the model file digest, the chosen SVM hyperparameters and the class fractions of the training labels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.model_pars_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.predict_labels-Tuple{LegendMLModel, AbstractMatrix}","page":"API","text":"predict_labels(m::LegendMLModel, X::AbstractMatrix) -> Vector{Int}\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.predict_labels"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.predict_with_margin-Tuple{LegendMLModel, AbstractMatrix}","page":"API","text":"predict_with_margin(m::LegendMLModel, X_or_wvfs) -> (labels, margin)\n\nLabels and the probability of the predicted class. Only defined for models trained with probability = true.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.predict_with_margin"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.propagate_labels-Tuple{ClusterResult, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}","page":"API","text":"propagate_labels(cluster::ClusterResult, exemplar_labels) -> Vector{Int}\n\nLabel of every sample row, taken from the label of its cluster's exemplar. Throws if any exemplar is still UNLABELED: training must never run on partially labeled clusters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.propagate_labels"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.qc_categories-Tuple{PropDicts.PropDict}","page":"API","text":"qc_categories(config::PropDict) -> Dict{Int,Symbol}\n\nCategory table from the categories section of the QC ML config.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.qc_categories"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.qc_ml_pars-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.LegendData, LegendDataManagement.FileKey}","page":"API","text":"qc_ml_pars(data, filekey) -> Union{PropDict, Nothing}\n\nParameter entry of the QC model valid for filekey (rpars.ml), resolved through the validity database. nothing when the rpars/ml directory does not exist, or no validity entry of it covers filekey.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.qc_ml_pars"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.qc_model_filename-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API","text":"qc_model_filename(sample_path) -> String\nqc_model_filename(data, fk) -> String\n\nJLD2 model file next to the sample file, same stem.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.qc_model_filename"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.qc_pars_entry_name-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.FileKey}","page":"API","text":"qc_pars_entry_name(fk) -> String\n\nPath of the rpars.ml entry of fk relative to the props-DB directory. One file per run and category, so the cal and the phy model of a run keep their own entry. It names both the file the entry is written to and the apply path of its validity record.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.qc_pars_entry_name"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.qc_sample_filename-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.LegendData, LegendDataManagement.FileKey}","page":"API","text":"qc_sample_filename(data, fk) -> String\n\nLH5 file of the training sample: the jlqml tier file of the training run's start key.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.qc_sample_filename"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.raw_filekeys-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.LegendData, LegendDataManagement.DataPeriod, LegendDataManagement.DataCategory}","page":"API","text":"raw_filekeys(data, period, category) -> Vector{FileKey}\n\nRaw filekeys of every analysis run of period in category, in run order. A run that runinfo lists but whose raw directory is absent or empty is skipped with a warning; an empty result is an error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.raw_filekeys"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.read_sample-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API","text":"read_sample(path) -> (sample, assignment, exemplars, stats)\n\nstats is the table written with the sample, or nothing for a file without one.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.read_sample"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.rule_predicate-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API","text":"rule_predicate(expr::AbstractString) -> Function\n\nPredicate of a selection rule written as a LEGEND Julia expression over the column names of a candidate table, e.g. \"daqenergy > 0 && tail_tau < 2000us\"; unit literals such as us and ns are understood (see LegendDataManagement.ljl_propfunc). The returned function maps a table to one result per row.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.rule_predicate"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.run_qc_sampling-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.LegendData, LegendDataManagement.FileKey, PropDicts.PropDict}","page":"API","text":"run_qc_sampling(data, training_fk, config; rng, filekeys, kwargs...) -> (sample, cluster, pars, scan)\n\nBuild the training sample of the period and category of training_fk from the raw files filekeys, scan and fit affinity propagation, write the jlqml sample file (with the rule inputs of the sample rows as its stats table), and return the parameter entry (with exemplar_labels initialized to UNLABELED) and the scan report. The entry's sample section records, per detector, the number of scan rows (n_scan) and how many of them each rule selects (n_matched). kwargs are forwarded to build_sample (e.g. chinfo to run without a channel map).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.run_qc_sampling"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.run_qc_training-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.LegendData, LegendDataManagement.FileKey, PropDicts.PropDict, PropDicts.PropDict}","page":"API","text":"run_qc_training(data, training_fk, config, pars; rng) -> (model, pars_entry, report)\n\nTrain the SVM from the labeled sample of training_fk, write the JLD2 model file and return the parameter entry to store under rpars.ml. training_fk names the model, independent of which sample rows happened to be drawn.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.run_qc_training"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.save_model-Tuple{AbstractString, LegendMLModel}","page":"API","text":"save_model(path, m::LegendMLModel) -> sha256::String\n\nWrite the model as JLD2: the machine in its serializable form, the feature extractor, the category table, the metadata, and MODEL_FORMAT_VERSION. Returns the SHA-256 of the written file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.save_model"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.scan_affinity_propagation-Tuple{AbstractMatrix}","page":"API","text":"scan_affinity_propagation(X; damp, preference_quantile, target_n_clusters=100, maxiter=1000, tol=1e-6, metric=Cityblock(), rng=Random.default_rng())\n\nRun affinity propagation on every (preference, damp) grid point and pick the converged one whose cluster count is closest to target_n_clusters, fewest iterations on ties. Grid points share one similarity matrix and run sequentially: each cell's working set is four n×n matrices, so cells cannot run concurrently without either racing on the shared matrix or multiplying that memory by the number of threads. The shared matrix's diagonal is overwritten with the grid point's preference before each call, so it never holds a specific preference once the scan returns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.scan_affinity_propagation"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.scan_candidates-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.LegendData, AbstractVector{LegendDataManagement.FileKey}, LegendDataManagement.DetectorId, Any}","page":"API","text":"scan_candidates(data, filekeys, det, aux_triggers; ts_window) -> TypedTables.Table\n\nRow scalars of every raw event of det in filekeys: filekey, eventnumber, timestamp, daqenergy, baseline, and the DAQ's counts of samples saturated at the low and high end of the ADC range, t_sat_lo and t_sat_hi, plus one Bool column per entry of aux_triggers (name => DetectorId pairs or a dictionary of them), e.g. :pulser => DetectorId(:PULS01). A flag is true where that aux channel has a triggered event (daqenergy > 0) within ts_window of the row's timestamp, the same coincidence the hit tier uses to mark pulser events.\n\nMatching by time rather than by row works in both categories: a cal file stores only the channels that fired, so an aux channel there holds its own triggers and its own row count, while a phy file writes every DAQ event to every channel.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.scan_candidates"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.scan_rows-Tuple{Any, Integer, Random.AbstractRNG}","page":"API","text":"scan_rows(daqenergy, n, rng) -> Vector{Int}\n\nSorted indices of min(n, length(daqenergy)) rows: rows with daqenergy > 0 drawn uniformly first, then, if those run out, rows with daqenergy <= 0. In a phy pool almost every row is an untriggered read with daqenergy == 0, and a uniform draw would leave the waveform rules few triggered events to act on.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.scan_rows"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.select_indices-Tuple{Any, Integer}","page":"API","text":"select_indices(cand, n; rules, uniform, rng) -> (idx, stratum)\n\nSorted row indices of the candidate table cand together with the name of the stratum each one was drawn by, length(idx) == min(n, length(cand)).\n\nrules is a sequence of (name::Symbol, select, fraction) in which select(cand) gives one Bool per row of cand; a missing or NaN result counts as false. The rules are drawn in order, without replacement and each only from rows the earlier ones left, up to round(Int, fraction * n) rows each; a rule with fewer rows than its quota gives what it has and leaves the rest of its share to the later strata. :uniform then fills the rest of n from the rows for which uniform(cand) is true, and :top_up from any rows still left.\n\nn at or above length(cand) returns every row, labeled by the first rule it matches, else :uniform or :top_up.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.select_indices"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.svm_grid-Tuple{PropDicts.PropDict}","page":"API","text":"svm_grid(svm_config::PropDict) -> (costs, gammas)\n\nLog-spaced tuning grids from the cost and gamma sections (min, max, n).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.svm_grid"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.train_svm-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}, PropDicts.PropDict}","page":"API","text":"train_svm(X, y, svm_config; groups, rng) -> (machine, report)\n\nGrid search over cost × gamma with stratified n_folds cross-validation on balanced accuracy, then a refit on all data with the best pair. The report holds the grid scores, a holdout confusion matrix (20 % stratified split), per-class and per-group accuracy. groups (e.g. detector types) must be index-aligned with y. class_accuracy[i] is missing, not 0, when classes[i] has no rows in the holdout split.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.train_svm"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.training_filekey-Tuple{LegendDataManagement.LegendData, LegendDataManagement.DataPeriod, LegendDataManagement.DataCategory}","page":"API","text":"training_filekey(data, period, category) -> FileKey\n\nStart key of the first analysis run of period for category.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.training_filekey"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.waveform_stats-Tuple{StructArrays.StructArray{<:RadiationDetectorSignals.RDWaveform{T, U, TV, UV} where {TV<:AbstractVector{T}, UV<:AbstractVector{U}}, N, @NamedTuple{time::VVT, signal::VVU}} where {T<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, U<:Union{Real, Unitful.AbstractQuantity{<:Real}}, N, VVT<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{T}}), VVU<:(AbstractVector{<:AbstractVector{U}})}}","page":"API","text":"waveform_stats(wvfs::ArrayOfRDWaveforms; bl_window, tail_window,\n               trigger_threshold=5, trigger_mintot=2.0u\"µs\", tx_mintot=32.0u\"ns\") -> TypedTables.Table\n\nOne row of summary statistics per waveform, computed from the trace as recorded (no pole-zero correction):\n\nblmean, blsigma, blslope, bl_slope_sigma: mean, standard deviation, fitted slope and standard deviation about the fitted line over bl_window, as the DSP's blmean, blsigma, blslope and bl_slope_sigma;\ntailmean, tailsigma, tailslope: the same over tail_window of the baseline-subtracted trace, and tail_tau = -tailmean / tailslope in µs, the decay time of an exponential with that mean and slope; a flat or rising tail gives a non-finite or negative value;\nwf_max, wf_min: extrema of the baseline-subtracted trace, amplitude = wf_max;\nt10, t50, t90: first crossings of 10, 50 and 90 % of wf_max that stay above for at least tx_mintot, NaN when there is none; risetime = t90 - t10;\nn_triggers: in-trace trigger multiplicity, counted as LegendDSP.get_triggers counts in-trace pile-up on the trace after a 2 µs rise, 1 µs flat-top trapezoidal filter: crossings of trigger_threshold times the sigma of the filtered trace over bl_window (measured from the start of the filtered trace) that last at least trigger_mintot.\n\nThe waveforms are processed in blocks, so the baseline-subtracted and filtered copies never exist for the whole array at once.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.waveform_stats"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#LegendMachineLearning.write_sample-Tuple{AbstractString, WaveformSample, ClusterResult}","page":"API","text":"write_sample(path, s::WaveformSample, c::ClusterResult; stats=nothing)\n\nLH5 layout: table sample and arrays clustering/assignment, clustering/exemplars, and, when stats is given, the table stats with one row per sample row (e.g. the rule inputs build_sample returns). Identifiers and stratum names are stored as strings; hyperparameters and convergence go to the parameter database (see cluster_result_to_props).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LegendMachineLearning.write_sample"},{"category":"section","location":"LICENSE/#LICENSE","page":"LICENSE","text":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2025 Oliver Schulz <oschulz@mpp.mpg.de>, Florian Henkes <florian.henkes@tum.de>, and contributors\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.\n\n","title":"LICENSE"},{"category":"section","location":"#LegendMachineLearning.jl","page":"Home","text":"","title":"LegendMachineLearning.jl"}]
